WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:10.129
Steve plugs the Core in by the desk
lamp, and Jean presses the button.

2
00:00:10.129 --> 00:00:14.000
It wakes and opens its own Wi-Fi network.

3
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:19.056
Jean joins the Core’s own network
from her phone’s Wi-Fi settings.

4
00:00:19.056 --> 00:00:21.900
Then she picks the home network.

5
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:26.588
Sally names her agent Juniper
and sends a first message.

6
00:00:26.588 --> 00:00:29.870
A reply comes back, the Core beside her.

7
00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:34.150
<v Juniper>Hello, Sally. I am Juniper.
Where shall we begin?

8
00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:37.226
One scan holds two clients’ papers.

9
00:00:37.226 --> 00:00:40.445
Sally splits it in
Stirling-PDF on the Core,

10
00:00:40.445 --> 00:00:44.050
so each client gets only their own pages.

11
00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:48.555
John’s book catalogue no
longer lives on one laptop.

12
00:00:48.555 --> 00:00:55.200
Code Server keeps it on the Core, so the
editor tab follows him to the loveseat.

13
00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:59.738
Upstairs, Steve signs in
to his own Valve account.

14
00:00:59.738 --> 00:01:06.750
The session itself runs on the Core in the
library, and he plays it in a browser.

15
00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:11.410
The page Jean quoted has
changed since she read it.

16
00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:17.850
Her Linkwarden copy, a screenshot and
a PDF, is the page as she read it.

17
00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:22.386
From the library to the pool,
one Companion Core serves

18
00:01:22.386 --> 00:01:26.950
the house, and the shelves
are still lined with books.

19
00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.971
Sally’s client folders,
John’s code and Jean’s

20
00:01:30.971 --> 00:01:33.737
sources sit on a Companion Core at home.

21
00:01:33.737 --> 00:01:37.718
Browse the Companion Hub store
and choose your first apps.

22
00:01:37.718 --> 00:01:39.600
UnCloud your life.
